      "content": "Taking your own life is not a compassionate act, because you deserve to live your own life even when it is painful. Self-sabotaging through this method would only define your relationship by your illness and pain, which is not what true selfless sacrifice looks like. Your partner is often resilient and finding ways to support you, even when it feels impossible, so consider seeking specialized help for this intrusive thought immediately. You do not have to disappear for them to survive; there is hope for both of you to find peace together with professional support.",
